From: superslor <289523157+superslor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:29:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] speculative: sampled MTP drafts verified with the
 speculative-sampling rule

From Kmic-68/llama.cpp dbe945b03 (MIT). LLAMA_SPEC_SAMPLE_TEMP=T samples each MTP draft token from its top
candidates (LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_TOPK, default 10) at temperature T and records the distribution; the server
verifies with min(1, p/q), else draws from the normalized residual, so the output distribution is the
target's. Only for requests that sample; greedy requests keep argmax drafts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
